In article <2g8t3iINN1sg0@rs1.rrz.Uni-Koeln.DE>, aus001@rrz.uni-koeln.de (Dionisius) writes:
>Regarding the luckstone characteristics:
>
>   State  |     Preserves        | Influence on
> of Stone | good luck | bad luck | actual luck
>----------+-----------+----------+---------------
>   cursed |    No     |   Yes    |   -1  
>----------+-----------+----------+---------------
> uncursed |   Yes     |   Yes    |   +1
>----------+-----------+----------+---------------
>  blessed |   Yes     |   No     |   +1
>
>The influence on the luck are cumulative (i.e. having 3 luckstones, blessed
>or uncursed, will increase your luck by 3). And, note that at full moon
>the influences are tripled (i.e. then *one* cursed luckstone will decrease
>your luck by 3). And note also that in no case the offset created by
>luckstones can be greater than +/- 3.

Nice table.  It's wrong though (at least for nethack 3.1.3, and all the
other versions I'm familiar with).  Having more than one luckstone has
no additional benefit.  You just get the effect of the best one in your
inventory.  Keeping a spare one in your bag of holding might be a good 
idea.  The table should look like this:

   State  |     Preserves        | Influence on
 of Stone | good luck | bad luck | actual luck
----------+-----------+----------+---------------
   cursed |    No     |   Yes    |   -3  
----------+-----------+----------+---------------
 uncursed |   Yes     |   Yes    |   +3
----------+-----------+----------+---------------
  blessed |   Yes     |   No     |   +3

